  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp; group attached with carbonyl bond will decrease reactivity of acid derivative towards hydrolysis. For halogen&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>&nbsp;dominate over&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;therefore, acid chloride is most reactive. As extent of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;effect&nbsp;increases, reactivity decreases. Overall, order of reactivity is:<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/56ba87b0-a548-4ac8-8b12-0d37a5d31f1d-image.png\" style=\"width: 483px; height: 141px;\" />",
